; The Lwt transport. Functorised over Mirage_flow.S rather than bound to a socket API,
; so the same code runs over TCP, over vsock, or over TLS in a MirageOS/Solo5
; unikernel. Nothing here may depend on unix -- that is mpc-unix's job, and only its
; job.
;
; Lwt rather than Eio is a constraint, not a preference: MirageOS has no Eio backend,
; so a unikernel-capable transport has to be Lwt-based.

(library
 (name mpc_lwt)
 (public_name mpc-lwt)
 (libraries mpc mpc.frost lwt cstruct mirage-flow mirage-crypto logs fmt))
